-\noindent\textbf{Abstract}\hspace{0.7em}The Galactic 511 keV annihilation emission is dominated by extended bulge and disk components, whereas the strength of any compact or point-like contribution remains uncertain. Pointed focusing observations can probe this complementary regime, but only when the atmospheric and instrument-induced backgrounds at balloon altitude are well controlled. We present a detector-coupled Monte Carlo estimate for a balloon-borne telescope that combines a 10 m Ge(111) Laue lens with a transition-edge sensor (TES) microcalorimeter focal plane. In the signal chain, the Laue optics first generate the focused focal-plane phase space for a monochromatic on-axis 511 keV point source, and photons passing the Be entrance aperture are then replayed through the detector/cryostat mass model. In the background chain, prompt atmospheric particles and photons and delayed activation decays are transported through the same detector/cryostat model; the delayed decays are seeded from the radionuclide-production positions recorded during the activation calculation. The resulting detector-level event streams are analyzed with the same $510.58$--$511.42\keV$ energy window, CsI anticoincidence veto, and topology/field-of-view consistency selection. For an incident point-source flux of $10^{-4}\phcms$, the selected day-15 signal and background rates are $1.19\times10^{-3}\cps$ and $3.92\times10^{-2}\cps$, respectively, and prompt atmospheric events account for 93.4\% of the selected background. Folding these rates through the adopted synthetic 20 d trajectory under continuous on-source exposure yields a diagnostic counting significance of $Z_{20\mathrm{d}}=7.80$ and a corresponding $3\sigma$ flux threshold of $3.85\times10^{-5}\phcms$. This threshold provides a flight-sensitivity estimate for a spectrally unresolved 511 keV point source under the reference model; the selected background is dominated by the prompt atmospheric component, which points to the shielding, collimation, and material choices most relevant to design optimization.
